IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ba-house`
IMPORT `ba-qa`

-- Building Act 2011 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (ba-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role and every
-- situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the roles it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error ("it
-- is an assumed term"). Each question that takes a situation input is asked, for its own role, with the situation FALSE
-- and every later input ASSUMEd: the answer must be `does not arise for you`. Both situation inputs are BOOLEANs, so no
-- helper reads a situation enumeration through OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31). Where a role's branch passes a fixed
-- Person and does not read the asker's own, that input is ASSUMEd too.
--
-- For the baseline's seat (the owner) each question is asked on the baseline's own facts, with the answer the baseline's
-- case file asserts, worked by hand from the text, and checked equal to the baseline export's answer on the same facts.
-- The builder's and the occupier's answers are worked by hand from ss 9, 16(c), 28(1)(a), 32, 33, 34(3), 37(1), 40, 41
-- and 133.
--
-- Facts from the WA lives: c055 (2029-07-15), Chloe and Liam's new house in Byford, built under a building permit by a
-- registered builder. That the regulations exempt the house from s 41 is asserted both ways, as in the baseline.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked person` IS A Person
ASSUME `unasked work` IS A `My work`
ASSUME `an unasked surveyor` IS A Surveyor
ASSUME `an unasked building` IS A Building
ASSUME `an unasked application kind` IS A `Kind of application`
ASSUME `an unasked permit application` IS A `My permit application`
ASSUME `an unasked occupancy application` IS A `Kind of occupancy permit application`
ASSUME `an unasked offence` IS A `My offence`

`as the owner` MEANS `I own the land the building is on, or will be on`
`as the builder` MEANS `I am the builder named on the building permit`
`as the occupier` MEANS `I live in or use the building as a tenant or licensee`

§§ `Fixtures (the baseline's)`

`Chloe, a registered proprietor of the Byford lot` MEANS Person WITH
    `is registered as a proprietor of the land` IS TRUE
    `holds a prescribed interest in the land` IS FALSE
    `is named as the builder on the building permit` IS FALSE

`the builder named on Chloe's permit` MEANS Person WITH
    `is registered as a proprietor of the land` IS FALSE
    `holds a prescribed interest in the land` IS FALSE
    `is named as the builder on the building permit` IS TRUE

`a tenant renting the house` MEANS Person WITH
