§§ `For the owner, and for the builder`

-- s 3: building a new house is building work; demolition is not.
#ASSERT `Is what I plan to do building work` `as the owner` `c055: the new Byford house, built under a building permit, as asked` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is what I plan to do building work` `as the builder` `demolishing the old house, as asked` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is what I plan to do building work` `as the owner` `demolishing the old house, as asked` EQUALS `yes if` (`Is it building work` `demolishing the old house`)
#ASSERT `Is what I plan to do building work` `as the occupier` `unasked work` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- s 9, s 69: a new house needs a permit; a garden shed the regulations exempt does not; a site office up three weeks
-- and closed to the public does not; a display home open to the public does; work under a building order does not.
#ASSERT `Does this work need a building permit` `as the owner` `c055: the new Byford house, built under a building permit, as asked` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Does this work need a building permit` `as the owner` `a garden shed the regulations exempt, as asked` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does this work need a building permit` `as the builder` `a site office up for three weeks, closed to the public, as asked` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does this work need a building permit` `as the builder` `a display home up for three weeks, open to the public, as asked` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Does this work need a building permit` `as the owner` `rectification work under a building order, as asked` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does this work need a building permit` `as the owner` `a display home up for three weeks, open to the public, as asked` EQUALS `yes if` (`Do I need a building permit` `a display home up for three weeks, open to the public`)
#ASSERT `Does this work need a building permit` `as the owner` `a site office up for three weeks, closed to the public, as asked` EQUALS `yes if` (`Do I need a building permit` `a site office up for three weeks, closed to the public`)
#ASSERT `Does this work need a building permit` `as the occupier` `unasked work` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- s 9, s 11: building the house with no permit is the offence, for the owner and for the builder who does it; with a
-- permit it is not; with a suspension the owner could not have known of, the s 11 defence.
#ASSERT `Would this work be the offence of building without a permit` `as the owner` `the Byford house built with no permit, as asked` FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Would this work be the offence of building without a permit` `as the builder` `the Byford house built with no permit, as asked` FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Would this work be the offence of building without a permit` `as the builder` `c055: the new Byford house, built under a building permit, as asked` FALSE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Would this work be the offence of building without a permit` `as the owner` `the Byford house built with no permit, as asked` TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Would this work be the offence of building without a permit` `as the owner` `the Byford house built with no permit, as asked` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Would doing the work be an offence` `the Byford house built with no permit` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Would this work be the offence of building without a permit` `as the occupier` `unasked work` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- s 4: an independent private surveyor: yes; one employed by the builder: no.
#ASSERT `Is the building surveyor independent` `as the owner` `an independent private building surveyor` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is the building surveyor independent` `as the builder` `a building surveyor employed by the builder` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is the building surveyor independent` `as the owner` `a building surveyor employed by the builder` EQUALS `yes if` (`Is my building surveyor independent` `a building surveyor employed by the builder`)
#ASSERT `Is the building surveyor independent` `as the occupier` `an unasked surveyor` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- s 16(b), (c): Chloe signs as an owner; the builder signs as the proposed builder (their own Person is not asked); a
-- tenant asked as an owner-seat person is not an owner and does not sign.
#ASSERT `Must I sign the application for the building permit` `as the owner` `Chloe, a registered proprietor of the Byford lot` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Must I sign the application for the building permit` `as the owner` `a tenant renting the house` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Must I sign the application for the building permit` `as the builder` `an unasked person` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Must I sign the application for the building permit` `as the owner` `Chloe, a registered proprietor of the Byford lot` EQUALS `yes if` (`Must I sign the building permit application` `Chloe, a registered proprietor of the Byford lot`)
#ASSERT `Must I sign the application for the building permit` `as the builder` `an unasked person` EQUALS `yes if` (`Must I sign the building permit application` `the builder named on Chloe's permit`)
#ASSERT `Must I sign the application for the building permit` `as the occupier` `an unasked person` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- s 28(1): the permit goes to each owner and to the named builder.
#ASSERT `Must I be given the building permit document` `as the owner` `Chloe, a registered proprietor of the Byford lot` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Must I be given the building permit document` `as the builder` `an unasked person` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Must I be given the building permit document` `as the owner` `a tenant renting the house` EQUALS `yes if` (`Must I be given the building permit` `a tenant renting the house`)
#ASSERT `Must I be given the building permit document` `as the occupier` `an unasked person` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- s 32: no period stated, 2 years; 3 years stated, 3.
#ASSERT `For how many years does the building permit have effect` `as the owner` 0 EQUALS years 2
#ASSERT `For how many years does the building permit have effect` `as the builder` 3 EQUALS years 3
#ASSERT `For how many years does the building permit have effect` `as the owner` 0 EQUALS years (`For how many years does my building permit last` 0)
#ASSERT `For how many years does the building permit have effect` `as the occupier` `an unasked number` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- s 33: the named builder, 7 days; Chloe, not the builder, 0 (not her duty); the fine $10 000.
#ASSERT `Within how many days of completion must I give notice of completion` `as the builder` `an unasked person` EQUALS days 7
#ASSERT `Within how many days of completion must I give notice of completion` `as the owner` `Chloe, a registered proprietor of the Byford lot` EQUALS days 0
#ASSERT `Within how many days of completion must I give notice of completion` `as the owner` `Chloe, a registered proprietor of the Byford lot` EQUALS days (`Within how many days must I give the notice of completion` `Chloe, a registered proprietor of the Byford lot`)
#ASSERT `Within how many days of completion must I give notice of completion` `as the builder` `an unasked person` EQUALS days (`Within how many days must I give the notice of completion` `the builder named on Chloe's permit`)
#ASSERT `Within how many days of completion must I give notice of completion` `as the occupier` `an unasked person` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for not giving notice of completion in time` `as the builder` EQUALS amount 10000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for not giving notice of completion in time` `as the owner` EQUALS amount `What is the most I can be fined for not giving notice of completion`
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for not giving notice of completion in time` `as the occupier` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- s 37: with a permit, the named builder answers for the standards and Chloe does not; without a permit, Chloe does
-- (s 37(2)) and the builder does not (s 37(1) needs a permit).
#ASSERT `Must I ensure the completed building meets the building standards` `as the builder` `an unasked person` `c055: the new Byford house, built under a building permit, as asked` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Must I ensure the completed building meets the building standards` `as the owner` `Chloe, a registered proprietor of the Byford lot` `c055: the new Byford house, built under a building permit, as asked` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Must I ensure the completed building meets the building standards` `as the owner` `Chloe, a registered proprietor of the Byford lot` `the Byford house built with no permit, as asked` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Must I ensure the completed building meets the building standards` `as the builder` `an unasked person` `the Byford house built with no permit, as asked` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Must I ensure the completed building meets the building standards` `as the owner` `Chloe, a registered proprietor of the Byford lot` `the Byford house built with no permit, as asked` EQUALS `yes if` (`Must I ensure the finished house meets the building standards` `Chloe, a registered proprietor of the Byford lot` `the Byford house built with no permit`)
#ASSERT `Must I ensure the completed building meets the building standards` `as the occupier` `an unasked person` `unasked work` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- s 34(3): the builder gives notice of cessation; the owner must get a copy within 7 days; the builder must give it
-- within 7 days, on a fine of $10 000. No notice of cessation: none of the three arises.
#ASSERT `Within how many days must I be given a copy of the notice of cessation` `as the owner` TRUE `Chloe, a registered proprietor of the Byford lot` EQUALS days 7
#ASSERT `Within how many days must I be given a copy of the notice of cessation` `as the owner` TRUE `Chloe, a registered proprietor of the Byford lot` EQUALS days (`Within how many days must I get the notice of cessation` `Chloe, a registered proprietor of the Byford lot`)
